{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/285779-wound-penalties-question","id":285779,"title":"wound penalties question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-18T01:46:14-07:00","id":285779,"title":"wound penalties question","content":"Reading the example of play in the V20 Dark Ages text, I noticed that wound penalties are used on damage rolls . Is this correct? I always assumed that a wound penalty already sort-of applied to damage by affecting the attack roll . It feels like double dipping to then use it on the damage roll. <br /> <br /> What rolls do you apply wound penalties to? <br /> <br /> As a secondary question, what rolls do you apply armor penalties to? Attack rolls, or just things like running and jumping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T17:48:09-07:00","id":286277,"title":"","content":"Never heard of them affecting Damage rolls since they're reflexive and all. Wouldn't make sense if they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523",